  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> The integrand is nonnegative and changes formula at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>. On the interval from 0 to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></math> its graph consists of two right triangles, each of base n and height 1. Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> The required sum is therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo>&#x022EF;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. It increases with positive integer n.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></math> the sum is 190, whereas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></math> it is 210. Equality is excluded by the strict inequality, so the largest permitted integer is 19. Answer C.</p>"
